# DJ Completeness (no stub features)

BananaLabs is a **full web DJ workstation** for human × AI co-performance. Capability stubs that look finished are bugs.

## Never claim / expose as done unless all three exist

1. **SetDoc + command** (typed mutation via `dispatch`)
2. **Audio/engine behavior** that actually performs it (not just stored state)
3. **Human booth UI** that can do the same action without JSON

If any of the three is missing, the feature is **incomplete** — finish it in the same pass or mark `debug-only` in the tool map with a one-line reason. Do not leave agent-only tools for core DJ features.

## Core DJ baseline (must work end-to-end)

When touching decks, mixer, set, or transport, ensure these are real — do not wait for the user to ask:

- Play/pause/seek (deck + **set performer** with transitions/automations)
- Tempo + **true keylock** (time-stretch, not `playbackRate` when keylock on)
- Loops (in + length; audio must reloop; UI pads; `loop_out` transition must hold a loop)
- Hotcues (set/trigger/clear + pads)
- EQ / filter / gain / faders / crossfader
- Arrangement trim, transitions, automation lanes
- FX, sampler, record (when in product scope — implement, don’t stub)
- **Share/Upload `.blset`** (SetDoc + audio round-trip for debugging)

## SoundTouch caveat

Prefer `@soundtouchjs/audio-worklet` (`SoundTouchNode`) for keylock. Mirror source `playbackRate` to the node and keep `pitch = 1`. Legacy ScriptProcessor `PitchShifter` is retired.

## Agent taste vs app mechanics

- Agent owns taste (what to play, where to mix, vibe).
- App owns mechanics (typed tools, no English parsing in `execute`, no “smart auto-DJ” that invents sets).
- Analysis has **no mix-in/out hints**. Agent chooses bars from sections/grid.

## Before finishing a feature PR

Ask: “Can a human do this from the booth UI the same way the agent does via WebMCP?” If no, add the UI.
